Chapter: GptArrayCrcGuardTest
  cites Works chapter GopFat16
  cites Works chapter GopXhci
  cites Foreword chapter Fat16
  cites Foreword chapter Gpt
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 The negative control for gpt-array-crc-ok. The .disk sidecar is the valid gop-fat16
 image with ONE change: One byte inside partition entry 5 is flipped, far past the two populated entries. The ESP entry is untouched, the geometry is untouched, the header CRC is untouched. The volume mounts and reads correctly in every other respect and the array CRC is the ONLY thing in the system that notices, which is the case a tampered ESP start LBA pointing at a DIFFERENT well-formed FAT would take.

 Ablate gpt-array-crc-ok and this flips to esp-start=64: the entry array no longer hashes to the value the header records, and the table is
 accepted anyway.

Section: Main

  show-esp : [Device.Port] Text
  show-esp = act
    s <- gpt-esp-start
    "esp-start=" & show s & " stage=" & show (xdiag-get gfat-cell-stage)
  end

  opening : [Console, Device.Port] Nothing = act
    a <- show-esp
    print-line-uni a
  end